 "limits": [
  "Synthetic workload and synthetic model on one machine over Docker networking; not a production capacity claim.",
  "15-second runs on fresh databases do not exercise table growth, so they cannot show the effect of the V3/V4 indexes; that evidence stays in bench/full_path_followup_2026-10-22.json.",
  "Three repeats per cell; medians and ranges are reported, no confidence intervals.",
  "The 750/s and 1,000/s runs are single exploratory runs."
 ],
 "decision": "compose.yaml now defaults to 4 scorer workers with 1 thread each (PAYGUARD_SCORE_WORKERS=4, PAYGUARD_SCORER_THREADS=1) and always starts the scorer with the TCP_NODELAY protocol. With the fix, 4x1 completed all 7,501 scheduled authorizations at 500/s in each of three runs (median p50 6.9 ms, p99 174 ms, 22-132 rules fallbacks), while 1 worker still saturated. Both variables can still be overridden.",
 "next_limit": "Single exploratory runs with 4x1 saturated at 750/s (about 680 completed per second, 1,017 dropped, 5% fallback) and at 1,000/s. Because fallback stayed low, the scorer deadline is not the main limit there; the API's 20-connection pool held during the scorer call, scorer CPU and PostgreSQL commit cost are the candidates. Not yet diagnosed.",
